# ==============================================================================
# 06_integrated_method_comparison.R
# ==============================================================================
#
# Project:
#   Pediatric appendicitis plasma miRNA-seq
#
# Purpose:
#   Integrate the complete differential-expression evidence generated by
#   scripts 04 and 05 across RPM/miRPM, edgeR-TMM and DESeq2.
#
# Role in pipeline:
#   Evidence integration and candidate prioritization.
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   This script does NOT use a predefined historical miRNA panel.
#   All miRNAs in the upstream-frozen feature set are integrated.
#
# Clinical variables inherited from script 01:
#   Appendicitis_status = NIA / Appendicitis
#   Phenotype           = NIA / Mild / Severe
#
# Prespecified analyses:
#   Appendicitis_vs_NIA
#   Phenotype_global
#   NIA_vs_Mild
#   NIA_vs_Severe
#   Mild_vs_Severe
#
# Methods:
#   RPM / miRPM:
#       supportive non-parametric evidence from script 04.
#
#   edgeR-TMM:
#       primary count-based validation from script 05.
#
#   DESeq2:
#       primary count-based validation from script 05.
#
# Models:
#   unadjusted:
#       primary count-based validation layer.
#
#   adjusted_age_sex:
#       sensitivity layer.
#
# Integration principles:
#
#   1. All methods are integrated on exactly the same upstream-filtered feature set.
#
#   2. For pairwise analyses, concordance requires the same effect direction.
#
#   3. Phenotype_global is an omnibus test and therefore has no unique
#      effect direction; direction is not required for its concordance.
#
#   4. FDR is interpreted within each original method x model x analysis.
#      No new p-value or artificial composite score is generated here.
#
#   5. The adjusted model is sensitivity evidence and does not create an
#      independent replicate. Robustness after age+sex adjustment is recorded
#      separately.
#
# Data-driven evidence classes:
#
#   FDR_concordant_robust:
#       edgeR and DESeq2 both have FDR < 0.05 for the same analysis, with
#       concordant direction when applicable, in BOTH unadjusted and age+sex
#       adjusted models.
#
#   FDR_cross_supported_robust:
#       at least one count method has FDR < 0.05 and the other is nominal
#       p < 0.05 for the same analysis, with concordant direction, in BOTH
#       unadjusted and age+sex adjusted models.
#
#   FDR_concordant_primary:
#       edgeR and DESeq2 both have FDR < 0.05 for the same analysis in the
#       unadjusted primary model, but the same evidence is not retained after
#       adjustment.
#
#   FDR_cross_supported_primary:
#       at least one count method has FDR < 0.05 and the other is nominal
#       p < 0.05 for the same analysis in the unadjusted primary model.
#
#   FDR_single_count_method:
#       at least one count-based method has FDR < 0.05 in the primary model,
#       without cross-method support at the same nominal threshold.
#
#   All_three_nominal_concordant:
#       RPM, edgeR and DESeq2 all have raw p < 0.05 for at least one same
#       analysis, with concordant direction when applicable.
#
#   Count_methods_nominal_concordant:
#       edgeR and DESeq2 both have raw p < 0.05 for at least one same analysis,
#       with concordant direction when applicable.
#
#   Other_nominal_signal:
#       nominal evidence exists but does not meet the above recurrence criteria.
#
#   No_integrated_signal:
#       no raw p < 0.05 in any primary method/analysis.
#
# NOTE:
#   These evidence classes are descriptive prioritization labels, not new
#   statistical significance tests.
#
# Visualization:
#   Integrated PCA/heatmaps are generated from log2(RPM + 1) only as a common
#   visualization scale after candidate definition.
#
#   These figures are post-selection and are NOT independent evidence.
#
# Main outputs:
#   results/<analysis_id>/integrated/
#
#     integrated_evidence_long.csv
#     integrated_candidate_summary_all_analyses.csv
#     integrated_candidate_summary_phenotype.csv
#     downstream_candidate_priority.csv
#     candidate_hierarchy_summary.csv
#     method_concordance_summary.csv
#     age_sex_stability.csv
#
#     candidates_count_nominal_concordant.csv
#     candidates_all_three_nominal_concordant.csv
#     candidates_primary_FDR_supported.csv
#     candidates_primary_FDR_cross_supported.csv
#     candidates_age_sex_robust_FDR.csv
#
#     integrated_manifest.csv
#     06_final_QC_summary.csv
#
# No sample or miRNA is removed in this script.
# ==============================================================================


